  "prompt": "# Adversarial code review \u2014 Offband caplog CLI verbs (#395)\n\nAdversarial embedded C++ review for **Offband** (MeshCore LoRa firmware, nRF52 + ESP32). Find\nbugs; don't praise. This slice adds the `caplog` CLI verbs on top of the already-merged\nserial-capture core (#393): `CaptureRing`/`MeshLog`.\n\nChanges in the diff below:\n- `CaptureRing::snapshot` gains an `offset` param for chunked reads (unit-tested).\n- `MeshLog` gains inline `meshLogLevelName`/`meshLogLevelFromName` (unit-tested) and\n  `meshLogDumpSerial()` (chunked stream to Serial).\n- `CommonCLI::handleCommand` gains `caplog start [level] / stop / erase / status / dump`.\n  Control + status are un-gated (bounded 160-byte replies, reachable over the companion/\n  authenticated channel); `caplog dump` is gated to the local console (`sender_timestamp == 0`).\n\nVerified: 14 native tests pass; builds on RAK4631 companion (nRF52) + Ebyte EoRa-S3 (ESP32-S3).\n\nReview concretely (cite file:line, rank by severity):\n\n1. **CLI dispatch correctness.** The verbs are an ordered `else if (memcmp(command, \"caplog X\", N))`\n   chain ending in a bare `\"caplog\"` (6). Any prefix cross-match, wrong ordering, or verb that\n   bare `\"caplog\"` wrongly swallows? Is the `caplog start <level>` arg parsing (`command[12]==' '`)\n   safe against short/malformed input and non-NUL-terminated buffers?\n2. **`meshLogDumpSerial()`** reads the ring in 128-byte chunks via `snapshot(\u2026, offset)`, each\n   under a brief lock, `Serial.write` between locks. If capture is still enabled and eviction\n   moves the tail mid-dump, what happens \u2014 duplication, skipping, infinite loop? Is that\n   acceptable for a \"best-effort local dump\", and is there any way it fails hard?\n3. **`CaptureRing::snapshot(offset)`** \u2014 bounds/wrap correctness with the new offset; any OOB read\n   or off-by-one when `offset` is near `bytesUsed()`?\n4. **Un-gating.** Control verbs now answer over the companion/authenticated channel. Any risk in\n   letting a remote caller enable/disable/erase capture or read `used/cap` status? Info leak?\n5. **Anything missed** \u2014 a data race, a `snprintf` size bug, a level-parse edge, or a simpler approach.\n\nBe terse. If fine, say so briefly.\n\n=== C:\\Users\\stryc\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Dev-meshcore-firmware\\ce5045af-5978-4a55-8b3c-9ce0975d4fe7\\scratchpad\\395-diff.txt ===\ndiff --git a/src/CaptureRing.cpp b/src/CaptureRing.cpp\nindex 97babfd0..fcd5ca2f 100644\n--- a/src/CaptureRing.cpp\n+++ b/src/CaptureRing.cpp\n@@ -53,10 +53,12 @@ size_t CaptureRing::bytesUsed() const { return _count; }\n \n size_t CaptureRing::capacity() const { return _cap; }\n \n-size_t CaptureRing::snapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap) const {\n-  size_t n = _count < out_cap ? _count : out_cap;\n+size_t CaptureRing::snapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap, size_t offset) const {\n+  if (offset >= _count) return 0;\n+  size_t avail = _count - offset;\n+  size_t n = avail < out_cap ? avail : out_cap;\n   for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n-    out[i] = _buf[ring_wrap(_tail + i, _cap)];\n+    out[i] = _buf[ring_wrap(_tail + offset + i, _cap)];\n   }\n   return n;\n }\ndiff --git a/src/CaptureRing.h b/src/CaptureRing.h\nindex e0a8d4f4..af2215ef 100644\n--- a/src/CaptureRing.h\n+++ b/src/CaptureRing.h\n@@ -31,8 +31,10 @@ public:\n   // Total capacity in bytes.\n   size_t capacity() const;\n \n-  // Copy up to out_cap bytes, oldest-first, into out. Returns bytes copied.\n-  size_t snapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap) const;\n+  // Copy up to out_cap bytes into out, oldest-first, starting `offset` bytes\n+  // from the oldest byte. Returns bytes copied (0 if offset >= bytesUsed()).\n+  // The offset lets the download path stream the buffer in chunks.\n+  size_t snapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap, size_t offset = 0) const;\n \n   // Drop all contents.\n   void clear();\ndiff --git a/src/MeshLog.cpp b/src/MeshLog.cpp\nindex eeae56c3..330a13a9 100644\n--- a/src/MeshLog.cpp\n+++ b/src/MeshLog.cpp\n@@ -78,6 +78,21 @@ size_t meshLogSnapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap) {\n   return n;\n }\n \n+void meshLogDumpSerial() {\n+  // Read in small chunks, each under a brief lock, writing to Serial between\n+  // locks so the critical section stays short (Serial writes can block).\n+  uint8_t chunk[128];\n+  size_t offset = 0;\n+  for (;;) {\n+    MLOG_ENTER();\n+    size_t n = g_ring.snapshot(chunk, sizeof(chunk), offset);\n+    MLOG_EXIT();\n+    if (n == 0) break;\n+    Serial.write(chunk, n);\n+    offset += n;\n+  }\n+}\n+\n void mesh_log_line(uint8_t level, const char* fmt, ...) {\n   // Cheap early-out: disabled by default, so stock builds pay one branch.\n   if (!g_meshLogEnabled || level > g_max_level) return;\ndiff --git a/src/MeshLog.h b/src/MeshLog.h\nindex d02a2b6f..6656b9ab 100644\n--- a/src/MeshLog.h\n+++ b/src/MeshLog.h\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n #pragma once\n #include <stdint.h>\n #include <stddef.h>\n+#include <string.h>\n \n // MeshLog \u2014 the serial-capture tee sink (#393).\n //\n@@ -28,6 +29,26 @@ enum MeshLogLevel : uint8_t {\n // Treat as read-only from producers; mutate only via meshLogSetEnabled().\n extern volatile bool g_meshLogEnabled;\n \n+// Level-name helpers for the `caplog` CLI (#395). Inline + Arduino-free so they\n+// are usable everywhere (including native unit tests) without linking MeshLog.cpp.\n+inline const char* meshLogLevelName(uint8_t level) {\n+  switch (level) {\n+    case MLOG_BOOT:   return \"boot\";\n+    case MLOG_ERROR:  return \"error\";\n+    case MLOG_DEBUG:  return \"debug\";\n+    case MLOG_PACKET: return \"packet\";\n+    default:          return \"?\";\n+  }\n+}\n+inline bool meshLogLevelFromName(const char* name, uint8_t* out_level) {\n+  if (!name || !out_level) return false;\n+  if (strcmp(name, \"boot\")   == 0) { *out_level = MLOG_BOOT;   return true; }\n+  if (strcmp(name, \"error\")  == 0) { *out_level = MLOG_ERROR;  return true; }\n+  if (strcmp(name, \"debug\")  == 0) { *out_level = MLOG_DEBUG;  return true; }\n+  if (strcmp(name, \"packet\") == 0) { *out_level = MLOG_PACKET; return true; }\n+  return false;\n+}\n+\n // Runtime control (wired to CLI verbs in #395).\n void   meshLogSetEnabled(bool enabled);   // default false\n bool   meshLogIsEnabled();\n@@ -38,6 +59,9 @@ size_t meshLogBytesUsed();\n size_t meshLogCapacity();\n // Copy up to out_cap captured bytes, oldest-first, into out (for #396 download).\n size_t meshLogSnapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap);\n+// Stream the captured buffer to Serial in chunks (local-console `caplog dump`).\n+// Best-effort: stop capture first for a clean dump. Framed remote download is #396.\n+void   meshLogDumpSerial();\n \n // The tee sink. printf-style; a \"\\n\"-terminated line is expected. No-op (cheap\n // early-out) when capture is disabled or the level is filtered out.\ndiff --git a/src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp b/src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp\nindex 82db5855..1190bf28 100644\n--- a/src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp\n+++ b/src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp\n@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@\n #include \"AdvertDataHelpers.h\"\n #include \"TxtDataHelpers.h\"\n #include <RTClib.h>\n+#include \"MeshLog.h\"   // serial-capture sink control (#395 caplog verbs)\n \n // Plan 2 v2 Task 11: ObserverCli dispatcher hooked into handleCommand's\n // fall-through. Compiles in only when OFFBAND_OBSERVER is defined\n@@ -741,6 +742,39 @@ void CommonCLI::handleCommand(uint32_t sender_timestamp, char* command, char* re\n     } else if (sender_timestamp == 0 && memcmp(command, \"log\", 3) == 0) {\n       _callbacks->dumpLogFile();\n       strcpy(reply, \"   EOF\");\n+    // #395: serial-capture (caplog). Control + status are un-gated (bounded\n+    // replies, safe over the companion/authenticated channel like `safety`);\n+    // the full `caplog dump` is local-console only (framed remote is #396).\n+    // Order: specific verbs before bare \"caplog\"; prefixes differ early so\n+    // memcmp lengths don't cross-match.\n+    } else if (memcmp(command, \"caplog start\", 12) == 0) {\n+      uint8_t lvl = MLOG_DEBUG;\n+      bool ok = true;\n+      if (command[12] == ' ' && command[13] != 0) {\n+        ok = meshLogLevelFromName(&command[13], &lvl);\n+      }\n+      if (!ok) {\n+        strcpy(reply, \"ERR: level = boot|error|debug|packet\");\n+      } else {\n+        meshLogSetLevel(lvl);\n+        meshLogSetEnabled(true);\n+        snprintf(reply, 160, \"caplog on (level %s)\", meshLogLevelName(lvl));\n+      }\n+    } else if (memcmp(command, \"caplog stop\", 11) == 0) {\n+      meshLogSetEnabled(false);\n+      strcpy(reply, \"caplog off\");\n+    } else if (memcmp(command, \"caplog erase\", 12) == 0) {\n+      meshLogClear();\n+      strcpy(reply, \"caplog erased\");\n+    } else if (sender_timestamp == 0 && memcmp(command, \"caplog dump\", 11) == 0) {\n+      meshLogDumpSerial();\n+      strcpy(reply, \"   EOF\");\n+    } else if (memcmp(command, \"caplog\", 6) == 0) {\n+      // bare \"caplog\" and \"caplog status\" -> status snapshot\n+      snprintf(reply, 160, \"caplog: %s level=%s used=%u/%u\",\n+               meshLogIsEnabled() ? \"on\" : \"off\",\n+               meshLogLevelName(meshLogGetLevel()),\n+               (unsigned)meshLogBytesUsed(), (unsigned)meshLogCapacity());\n     } else if (sender_timestamp == 0 && memcmp(command, \"stats-packets\", 13) == 0 && (command[13] == 0 || command[13] == ' ')) {\n       _callbacks->formatPacketStatsReply(reply);\n     } else if (sender_timestamp == 0 && memcmp(command, \"stats-radio\", 11) == 0 && (command[11] == 0 || command[11] == ' ')) {\ndiff --git a/test/test_capture_ring/test_capture_ring.cpp b/test/test_capture_ring/test_capture_ring.cpp\nindex 372f6f86..4e80cdcc 100644\n--- a/test/test_capture_ring/test_capture_ring.cpp\n+++ b/test/test_capture_ring/test_capture_ring.cpp\n@@ -100,6 +100,36 @@ TEST(CaptureRing, SnapshotRespectsOutputCapacity) {\n   EXPECT_EQ(0, memcmp(out, \"abcd\", 4));   // oldest-first\n }\n \n+// Offset lets the download path read the buffer in chunks (#395 dump / #396).\n+TEST(CaptureRing, SnapshotFromOffsetReadsChunk) {\n+  uint8_t buf[64];\n+  CaptureRing r(buf, sizeof(buf));\n+  appendStr(r, \"0123456789\\n\");     // 11 bytes\n+  uint8_t out[4];\n+  size_t n = r.snapshot(out, sizeof(out), 4);  // 4 bytes from offset 4\n+  EXPECT_EQ(4u, n);\n+  EXPECT_EQ(0, memcmp(out, \"4567\", 4));\n+}\n+\n+TEST(CaptureRing, SnapshotOffsetAtOrBeyondEndReturnsZero) {\n+  uint8_t buf[64];\n+  CaptureRing r(buf, sizeof(buf));\n+  appendStr(r, \"abc\\n\");            // 4 bytes\n+  uint8_t out[8];\n+  EXPECT_EQ(0u, r.snapshot(out, sizeof(out), 4));   // offset == count\n+  EXPECT_EQ(0u, r.snapshot(out, sizeof(out), 10));  // offset past end\n+}\n+\n+TEST(CaptureRing, SnapshotOffsetClampsToRemaining) {\n+  uint8_t buf[64];\n+  CaptureRing r(buf, sizeof(buf));\n+  appendStr(r, \"hello\\n\");          // 6 bytes\n+  uint8_t out[16];\n+  size_t n = r.snapshot(out, sizeof(out), 3);  // only 3 bytes remain from offset 3\n+  EXPECT_EQ(3u, n);\n+  EXPECT_EQ(0, memcmp(out, \"lo\\n\", 3));\n+}\n+\n int main(int argc, char** argv) {\n   ::testing::InitGoogleTest(&argc, argv);\n   return RUN_ALL_TESTS();\ndiff --git a/test/test_meshlog_level/test_meshlog_level.cpp b/test/test_meshlog_level/test_meshlog_level.cpp\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..8f556808\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/test_meshlog_level/test_meshlog_level.cpp\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+// Native unit tests for the MeshLog verbosity level-name helpers (#395) used\n+// by the `caplog start [level]` CLI verb. Pure inline logic \u2014 no Arduino.\n+\n+#include <gtest/gtest.h>\n+#include \"MeshLog.h\"\n+\n+TEST(MeshLogLevel, NameForEachLevel) {\n+  EXPECT_STREQ(\"boot\", meshLogLevelName(MLOG_BOOT));\n+  EXPECT_STREQ(\"error\", meshLogLevelName(MLOG_ERROR));\n+  EXPECT_STREQ(\"debug\", meshLogLevelName(MLOG_DEBUG));\n+  EXPECT_STREQ(\"packet\", meshLogLevelName(MLOG_PACKET));\n+}\n+\n+TEST(MeshLogLevel, FromNameValid) {\n+  uint8_t lvl = 99;\n+  EXPECT_TRUE(meshLogLevelFromName(\"boot\", &lvl));\n+  EXPECT_EQ(MLOG_BOOT, lvl);\n+  EXPECT_TRUE(meshLogLevelFromName(\"packet\", &lvl));\n+  EXPECT_EQ(MLOG_PACKET, lvl);\n+}\n+\n+TEST(MeshLogLevel, FromNameInvalidLeavesOutputUnchanged) {\n+  uint8_t lvl = 42;\n+  EXPECT_FALSE(meshLogLevelFromName(\"bogus\", &lvl));\n+  EXPECT_EQ(42, lvl);\n+}\n+\n+int main(int argc, char** argv) {\n+  ::testing::InitGoogleTest(&argc, argv);\n+  return RUN_ALL_TESTS();\n+}\n\n\n",
  "response": "An adversarial review of the `caplog` CLI addition follows.\n\n### 1. High: CLI Prefix Matching Bug\n\n*   **`src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp:760, 763, 768`**\n*   The `memcmp` checks for `caplog stop`, `caplog erase`, and the bare `caplog` command do not verify that the command ends after the verb (with a NUL or space). This causes incorrect command matching. For example:\n    *   `caplog stop-something` is treated as `caplog stop`.\n    *   `caplog startle` is not matched by `caplog start` (correct) but falls through and is incorrectly matched by the bare `caplog` check, treating it as a status request.\n*   **Fix:** Add a terminator check, as is done for other commands in the same file:\n    ```cpp\n    // Example for 'caplog stop'\n    } else if (memcmp(command, \"caplog stop\", 11) == 0 && (command[11] == 0 || command[11] == ' ')) {\n    ```\n\n### 2. Medium: `caplog start` Argument Parsing Unsafe\n\n*   **`src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp:751-753`**\n*   The argument parsing for `caplog start <level>` is unsafe if the input buffer `command` is not NUL-terminated. The code checks `command[12] == ' '`, then passes `&command[13]` to `meshLogLevelFromName`, which calls `strcmp`. If the buffer contains `caplog start level` without a NUL terminator, `strcmp` will read out of bounds. While the surrounding infrastructure likely ensures NUL termination, this specific handler shouldn't rely on it.\n*   **Fix:** The command should be tokenized or a temporary, NUL-terminated buffer should be used for the argument.\n\n### 3. Low: `meshLogDumpSerial` Race Condition\n\n*   **`src/MeshLog.cpp:84`**\n*   The `meshLogDumpSerial` function reads the ring buffer in chunks, releasing the lock between each `Serial.write`. If new log entries are captured during the dump and cause old entries to be evicted, the `_tail` of the ring buffer will advance. The dumper's `offset` becomes stale relative to the new `_tail`, causing it to skip sections of the log.\n*   The comment acknowledges this is \"best-effort,\" and the implementation avoids deadlock or infinite loops. However, the data skipping behavior might be unexpected. It is an acceptable trade-off for keeping lock contention low, but it's a notable one.\n\n### 4. Low: Un-gated Control Verbs Risk\n\n*   **`src/helpers/CommonCLI.cpp:749-771`**\n*   The `caplog start/stop/erase/status` verbs are not gated to the local console (`sender_timestamp == 0`). This allows any authenticated node on the mesh to enable, disable, or wipe the log buffer on another node. This presents a denial-of-service vector for debugging; a remote peer could repeatedly erase logs, preventing a local operator from capturing a bug.\n*   While a design choice to allow remote control (e.g., from a companion app), the security/nuisance trade-off warrants consideration. At a minimum, `caplog erase` should be considered for local-only execution.\n\nThe logic in `CaptureRing::snapshot(offset)` appears correct and is well-tested. No other significant bugs were found."
